comments.body:
**Open sub-lemma, part (d).** The GRE/Lyapunov program requires:
(i) existence and positivity of the **dual** eigenfunction $\phi>0$ solving the formal adjoint of the operator in (a) with the same $\lambda$ (the operator is non-self-adjoint due to drift; existence again needs Krein–Rutman on the adjoint);
(ii) definition $\mathcal H[h\mid F]=\int \phi\,F\,H(h/F)\,dx$ for convex $H$, with $h=e^{-\lambda t}f$ the renormalized density;
(iii) the entropy-dissipation identity $\frac{d}{dt}\mathcal H = -\mathcal D\le0$ with $\mathcal D$ written explicitly, including justification that boundary terms at $\pm\infty$ vanish (uses decay of $F,\phi$);
(iv) a convergence statement $h\to \rho_\infty F$, with rate under a spectral-gap hypothesis (gap between $\lambda$ and the rest of the spectrum). All four steps must be carried out in full. Reference: Michel–Mischler–Perthame (2005).
